

### Relations with Theta Functions (chapter 16)

The formal definitions of the four \(\vartheta\) functions are given by the series 16.27.1-16.27.4 which converge for all complex \(z\) and all \(\vartheta\) defined below. (Some authors use \(\pi z\), instead of \(z\), as the independent variable.)

These functions depend on \(z\) and on a parameter \(q\), which is usually suppressed. Note that

\[\vartheta_{i}^{\prime}(0) = \vartheta_{2}(0)\vartheta_{3}(0)\vartheta_{4}(0),\]

where \(\vartheta_{i}(0) = \vartheta_{i}(0,\,\vartheta)\).

